        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Yellowcraig, Broad Sands Bay, East Lothian, Scotland, Firth of Forth, Dirleton\n- Landmarks: Dirleton Castle\n- Properties: North Berwick West Links golf course, Archerfield Estate, Links golf courses\n\nFacts:\n- Dirleton Castle is a medieval fortress in the village of Dirleton, East Lothian, Scotland.\n- The oldest parts of Dirleton Castle date to the 13th century.\n- Dirleton Castle was abandoned by the end of the 17th century.\n- Yellowcraig, less commonly known as Broad Sands Bay, is a coastal area of forest, beach, and grassland in East Lothian in south-east Scotland.\n- Yellowcraig is bordered to the north by the Firth of Forth.\n- Yellowcraig is bordered to the south by the village of Dirleton and Dirleton Castle.\n- Yellowcraig is bordered to the east by the North Berwick West Links golf course.\n- Yellowcraig is bordered to the west by the Archerfield Estate and Links golf courses.",
